        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">After <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3207883044\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40228\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/40228/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40228\">#40228</a>, we are a lot more explicit on some CSS stylistic decisions. This PR fixes two basic things: comments should start and end with a space, and the use of <code class=\"notranslate\">from</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">to</code> selectors should follow our style guide.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40608",
            "title": "Lint: spaces around CSS comments, from/to keyframe selectors",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-03T15:51:51.000Z",
