        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF142 <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Animation/commitStyles\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Animation/commitStyles()</code></a> allows animations to capture the final styles without specifying a <code class=\"notranslate\">fill</code> in latest spec.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note that normally I'd have the new behavior front and center and mention the older behavior as a legacy thing. Unfortunately the advice of the developer is that you can't feature check for this, so people will have to stick with the old behaviour until this is in most browsers.<br>\nSo this update covers the old case first, and puts the new information second.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3249106813\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40482\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/40482/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40482\">#40482</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40585",
            "title": "FF142 Animation.commitStyles() automatically fills values",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-04T01:51:19.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-01T07:24:15.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/112591951?u=83251e0d8e8f801faef99cc68533e148a728784b&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Corrects the Safari origin and overall storage quota values to match WebKit’s official policy and clarifies the distinction between browser apps, web apps, and non-browser WebViews, just as requested in the issue.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">As stated in the issue, the current numbers in the MDN documentation for Safari’s per-origin quota (20% vs 60%) and overall quota (15% vs 80%) were inverted and the role of WebViews versus standalone web apps was unclear. Updating these values ensures MDN reflects the current WebKit storage policy and prevents developers from planning around incorrect limits.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">The issue referenced pull request <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1846151273\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/28510\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/28510/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/28510\">#28510</a>, which uses the Webkit article and has the numbers flipped.<br>\nWebKit article: <a href=\"https://www.webkit.org/blog/14403/updates-to-storage-policy/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.webkit.org/blog/14403/updates-to-storage-policy/</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #40394.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3237705756\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40394\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/40394/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/40394\">#40394</a></p>\n\n\n\n",
